From b86029422e83af048171f39eba8b8412baf55934 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayesh Rathod <jayesh4.rathod@ril.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:18:05 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] Hull Pine: gateway admission and next-session paper
 fills

Steps 6 and 9 of the Cross-Scanner Eligibility and Corporate Lifecycle Sprint.

Hull Pine had the largest gap. It loaded every symbol with 300 sessions and
consulted no security master, no active flag, no series and no corporate
lifecycle, then booked a paper entry at the signal bar's own closing price --
a price no order could have been filled at. Its live state file shows the
result: 13 of 16 paper positions were ETFs and index funds.

Step 6 -- admission
-------------------
run_daily() now runs the shared gateway before any Hull metric and evaluates
only admitted symbols. On the real store at 2026-08-20 this removed JBCHEPHARM,
19 stale symbols, 103 non-EQ series and 101 restricted symbols, and labelled 228
ETFs observe-only.

Step 9 -- next-session fill
--------------------------
READY is now a *pending setup*, never a position:

  BUILD -> NEAR -> READY -> TRIGGERED -> ENTERED

* The entry range runs from the signal bar's own high to that high plus
  max_chase_atr (default 0.5) ATRs. Confirmation requires trade *above* the
  signal high, so the signal close can never be a fill.
* A later session fills at min(max(open, trigger), ceiling). A bar that opens
  beyond the ceiling is DECLINED as a chase rather than filled at an
  unobtainable price. A bar with no range is treated as circuit-locked and is
  not executable at any price. A fill that would sit below the structural stop
  is refused.
* Setups expire after setup_validity_sessions (default 5) or on a decline, and
  every transition is recorded in the state event log.

Legacy state
------------
STATE_VERSION moves 1 -> 2. load_state previously discarded any state whose
version did not match, so the bump alone would have silently wiped the existing
16-position track record; _migrate_state upgrades in place instead.

Per the decisions taken for this sprint:
* Existing entries are grandfathered and tagged fill_rule=SIGNAL_CLOSE_LEGACY.
  The next-session rule applies to new entries only; paper history is not
  retroactively rewritten.
* A position in a symbol that may no longer be entered is closed at its last
  price through v2/universe_reconciliation. On the live state this closed
  GSEC10IETF at 266.38 and MOMENTUM50 at 54.07 as UNIVERSE_EXIT /
  NON_EQ_UNVERIFIED_HOLDING, leaving the equity holdings untouched.

pine_metrics now also returns the signal bar's high and low, which the entry
range needs.

tests/test_pine_hull_engine.py::test_pine_daily_state_is_independent_and_freezes_entry_levels
asserted position["entry"] == 260.0 -- the same-close fill this step removes.
It is rewritten as test_ready_creates_a_pending_setup_and_never_a_same_close_entry,
and its fixture now creates a symbol_master_v2 row, because a symbol absent from
the master is correctly no longer enterable.

Tests: 19 new covering the trigger rule, the full lifecycle, gateway admission
and legacy holdings; 4 in the existing pine suite pass.
